    <h1>About LanDeng</h1>
    <p><em>Last updated: 2026-10-23 · Applies to incenseherbs.com and data.incenseherbs.com</em></p>

    <p class="lead">
      LanDeng (澜灯) is a research-led, English-language platform for Chinese botanical incense: its
      materials, botanicals, history, terminology, craft, and culture. It is the brand of
      <strong>Zhangjiakou Landeng Technology Co., Ltd.</strong>, a supplier of Chinese botanical
      incense. This page states who we are, what we publish, how we work, and — just as deliberately —
      what we do not claim.
    </p>

    <h2>What LanDeng is</h2>
    <p>
      LanDeng is two things at once, and it is honest about both. It is a <strong>knowledge
      platform</strong> — an ingredient encyclopedia, technique and history guides, and structured
      open datasets — and it is a <strong>manufacturer and supplier directory</strong> that connects
      readers to wholesale, OEM, and private-label work. The two halves share one rule: knowledge is
      documented with source transparency, and commercial claims are made only per inquiry, never as
      fabricated marketing.
    </p>
    <p>
      The name LanDeng (澜灯) means "lantern on the waves" — a soft glow over still water. It is the
      brand name under which the company publishes its editorial content and offers its products.
    </p>

    <h2>What we publish</h2>
    <p>The site is organized around a few clear strands:</p>
    <ul>
      <li>
        <strong>An ingredient encyclopedia</strong> — source-transparent entries for the woods, resins,
        flowers, herbs, and spices used in Chinese incense, each documenting identity, processing,
        grading, and safety, with an Evidence &amp; Sources section.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Guides and reference</strong> — the history of Chinese incense, the way of incense
        (香道), the 合香 blending system, technique guides, and business guides for buyers.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Structured open datasets</strong> — on data.incenseherbs.com, the same entities are
        published as machine-readable Schema.org datasets (ingredients, terminology, relationships,
        comparisons, materials, forms, techniques, and aroma families) under CC BY-SA 4.0.
      </li>
      <li>
        <strong>Commercial services</strong> — wholesale of existing products, OEM development to your
        specification, and private-label branding of existing products, arranged by email.
      </li>
    </ul>

